{"title":"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b8945a2aaa3228362b3976be341ad72f51f56efe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> be the number of ways of selecting three distinct numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d986c53a383b5ba42fa540ef8e51a344c94bbc06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{1, 2, 3,\\cdots ,n\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> so that they are\nthe lengths of the sides of a triangle. As an example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd955785f63023d8d3e19590707a02d101c8e97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(5) = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />; the only possibilities are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39658accb363573da22a55c4376e2ffb0ff00c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2-3-4\\},\\{ 2-4-5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />,\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/e/e1eb65703db19b3a0e5341155c1da6a4ac47bf7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{3-4-5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>(a) Determine a recursion for T(n).\n</p><p>(b) Determine a closed formula for T(n).\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a1f6feecc875aade28f69e75c71fe1e66d0e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(n+1)+T(n)=\\binom{n}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"189\" height=\"53\" /> \n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd2eb219751e72427538fb59c18ab9fbb21ddf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(N) = \\binom{N-1}{3}-\\binom{N-2}{3}+\\binom{N-3}{3}-\\binom{N-4}{3}+\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"481\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II\">2011 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed